WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.578
The training set is constructed entirely with JAM,

00:00:03.658 --> 00:00:06.724
the physics code SKiNN is meant to imitate.

00:00:06.804 --> 00:00:10.602
The authors created five thousand input-output pairs,

00:00:10.682 --> 00:00:15.138
using four thousand for training, five hundred for
validation,

00:00:15.218 --> 00:00:17.919
and five hundred held out for testing.

00:00:17.999 --> 00:00:20.919
Each velocity image is 551 by 551 pixels,

00:00:20.999 --> 00:00:24.284
generated at higher resolution than real data.

00:00:24.364 --> 00:00:28.747
Creating a single image with JAM takes about
fifteen seconds,

00:00:28.827 --> 00:00:32.113
which underscores why emulation is worthwhile.

00:00:32.193 --> 00:00:39.210
The network is implemented in PyTorch with PyTorch
Lightning and trained on five Tesla P100 GPUs,

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:43.600
each with sixteen gigabytes of memory, over roughly
one day.
